Subject: [PATCH] Frontier section: documentation amendments 445-A to 445-D
 from the classification review (#445 6138311227)

README.md and SCOPE.md only (identical edits in both): the vocabulary class and its 36 row
reasons describe reusable predicates used in definitions, hypotheses and conclusions, with
the counted examples, and label the 105/77/28 grouping as this section's planning convention
(445-A); the two Side24 rows read "conditioned on the pin V_u = H_f u = 0" (445-B); the
interface-blocked and Mathlib-blocked class texts and the B, C, E11, R1 and F4 rows separate
blocker judgement from impossibility and from each target's stated shape, with the
nonemptiness/vacuity qualifications, the non-kernel status of the refutations, the proof
machinery named as a route and not as conclusion conjuncts, and the conditional form of R1
(445-C); the R1 version remark is replaced by the reviewer's wording (445-D). No row is
promoted or moved between classes; counts unchanged (36 + 24 + 4 = 64; 64 + 77 = 141); no
register, module, gate or toolchain change.

Scientific effect: NONE. Organizational-independence credit 0.

